    "result": "I made the installed file mode 0755. The old code also failed on every second run, so I rewrote `install.go` so it can run any number of times. I could not compile or run it because the permission prompts for `go vet` were blocked.\n\n- **Second run:** it used `os.Mkdir` and `O_EXCL`, which fail when the directory or file already exists. It now uses `MkdirAll`. If the installed file already has the same bytes, it only sets the mode and changes nothing else.\n- **Crash during copy:** it now writes to a fixed temp name `.\u003cname\u003e.tmp` in the same folder, then renames that over the target. A reboot leaves either the old file or the new file, never half of one. The next run overwrites any leftover temp file.\n- **Mode:** it calls `Chmod` after the write, because the mode given at file creation is reduced by umask.\n\nNOTE: on Windows, the rename fails if the binary it replaces is running.",
